{#
  Bill Pay — Scene gallery accordion. Replaces the chrome around Gallery 1
  (caption row + progress bar + 650px mock) with a vertical accordion rail,
  per the "Volume_Productivity Gallery — Accordion Restructure" build spec.
  Does not touch the scenes themselves: the mock is the exact same
  continuous-timeline document (assets/scene-gallery/bill-pay/scenes.html)
  Gallery 1 already plays — this only changes what's wrapped around it. See
  js/bill-pay/scene-gallery-accordion.js for the postMessage protocol
  (identical shape to scene-gallery.js's, reused against the same iframe).

  scene-gallery.njk / scene-gallery.css / scene-gallery.js are superseded by
  this component and left in place, unreferenced — same pattern as
  scene-accordion.njk superseding accordion-gallery.njk.

  Tag markup/classes (.principles-tag / .principles-tag__label) are the
  exact ones Gallery 2 uses (css/components/principles.css) — reused, not
  duplicated, per CLAUDE.md's "reuse existing component CSS wherever
  possible."

  Layout: tag, then a row of [144px rail][50px gap][606px mock] — 800px
  total, the article's full content column (--sga-rail-width /
  --sga-mock-width, scene-gallery-accordion.css) — see that file's own
  comment on .scene-gallery-accordion for why the tag/arrow sit at a fixed
  -30px from this column's own left edge (matching Gallery 2's own
  --sg2-overhang value, not its rendered page position).

  Tag and mock share the same top
  anchor (the tag is positioned out of flow, at the outer wrapper's own
  top:0 — see the CSS); the rail alone starts --spacing-64 below that,
  via its own margin-top. This needs one shared wrapper (unlike an earlier
  build of this component, which relied on .section__slot's own gap between
  two top-level siblings) — that approach couldn't express "tag and mock
  share a top edge, rail doesn't" without hardcoding the tag's own rendered
  height, which this positioning avoids entirely.

  Standalone component — no section wrapper, no headline, no background.
  Caller drops {{ sceneGalleryAccordion() }} into its own content column.
#}
{% macro sceneGalleryAccordion() %}
<div class="scene-gallery-accordion">
  <div class="scene-gallery-accordion__tag">
    <div class="principles-tag"><p class="principles-tag__label"># Volume_Productivity</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="scene-gallery-accordion__row">
    <div class="scene-gallery-accordion__rail">
      <div class="scene-gallery-accordion__arrow" id="scene-gallery-accordion-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <ol class="scene-gallery-accordion__list" id="scene-gallery-accordion-list"></ol>
    </div>
    <div class="scene-gallery-accordion__mock">
      <iframe class="scene-gallery-accordion__visual" id="scene-gallery-accordion-visual" title="Bill Pay scene"></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
